    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493338060/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Saturday, Apr. 4, 1908
Paris with Scott.
Ray and Karin came to see us off at Victoria. It was  awful  parting with them. 
The crossing was rough, and I suffered from “deferred sea-sickness” all night.
The train was late and Neith and Hutch were waiting for us. We all went to dine at the Lapérouse, and Hutch gave us a lot of jaw about Topic No. I. Then they insisted on our going to a Café, where we sat very drearily until midnight, when they took the train for St. Cloud, and we went — oh so weary and sick! — to bed. Hutch was a great dear, all the same. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 117 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1908> .

